{"input_text": "Question: I'm trying to calculate the cardinality of these two sets. I think the answer is ℵ, and I want to prove it by finding proper injective functions, and using Schröder–Bernstein theorem. Any help will be much appreciated. 
 F = {f ∈ N → N |  f is a bijection} 
 G = {f ∈ N → N|f ◦ f = idN} 

Answer: Set $x=\tan\theta$, we have
$$I=\int_{0}^{\infty}{2x\over (x^2+1)(x^2+2)}dx=\int_{0}^{\frac{\pi}{2}}\frac{2\tan\theta(1+\tan^2\theta)}{(1+\tan^2\theta)(2+\tan^2\theta)}d\theta$$
